# Rename to .env.local (it is gitignored) and restart `npm run dev`.
#
# Free project id from https://dashboard.reown.com — required for WalletConnect
# QR pairing. Browser-extension wallets work without it.
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Builder fee (SoDEX builder codes) — OFF unless VITE_BUILDER_ID is set.
# Full description, and the live test to run before switching it on:
# docs/BUILDER-CODES.md
#
# With these unset nothing is approved, attached or shown: the app is exactly
# what it is without a builder. They are read at BUILD time (Vite), so a change
# needs a restart of `npm run dev` / a new build.
#
# The builder is a SoDEX trading account of yours that holds at least 100 vUSDC
# in Spot AND 100 vUSDC in Perps. Its numeric account id, a balance check and
# these lines filled in:
#   node tools/check-builder.mjs <builder wallet address> [--testnet]
#
# Fees are whole numbers in TENTHS OF A BASIS POINT: 10 = 1 bp = 0.01 % of a
# fill, 50 = 0.05 %. SoDEX charges them per fill, on top of its own fee, and
# credits them to the builder account.
#
# The builder account id. Unset = no builder fee.
# VITE_BUILDER_ID=
#
# Fee on every perps fill of an order placed here, buys and sells (0..200).
# VITE_BUILDER_FEE_PERPS=50
#
# Fee on every spot SELL fill of an order placed here (0..2000). SoDEX does not
# charge builder fees on spot buys.
# VITE_BUILDER_FEE_SPOT=50
#
# The maximum the user's wallet approves (0..2000). Default: the higher of the
# two fees. Raising a fee above an approved maximum makes every user approve
# again, so set it only as high as you intend to charge.
# VITE_BUILDER_MAX_FEE=50
#
# 1 = trading through Valuescan requires the approval: a user who declines
# cannot enable trading here. Unset (default) = optional: a user who declines,
# or whose approval SoDEX refuses, trades without a builder fee.
# VITE_BUILDER_REQUIRED=1
